{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-149622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}2{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-2)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{a}_{i}=42,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}{b}_{j}=70.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}2{a}_{i}({b}_{j}-2) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}2{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}({b}_{j}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}2{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}({b}_{j}-2) & =(2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}{b}_{j}-{\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}2) \\\\  & =(2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{a}_{i})\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}{b}_{j}-2{\\sum }_{j=1}^{30}1) \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 42)\\cdot (70-2\\cdot 30) \\\\  & =(84)\\cdot (70-60) \\\\  & =(84)\\cdot (10) \\\\  & =840\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149622" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "640efeb508dfb43c2554d4d361c3677898932e82d50175856399e8b5cf2882bb"} {"question" "q-149622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "320"] ["math" "480"] ["math" "760"] ["math" "840"] ["math" "960"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149622" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "840"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}=75,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij}=80.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(2{a}_{ij}-{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}2{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{30}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 75-80 \\\\  & =150-80 \\\\  & =70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149667" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "640efeb508dfb43c2554d4d361c3677898932e82d50175856399e8b5cf2882bb"} {"question" "q-149667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "60"] ["math" "65"] ["math" "70"] ["math" "75"] ["math" "80"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149667" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "70"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}{a}_{ij}=200,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}{b}_{ij}=175.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}{b}_{ij}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}1 \\\\  & =200+175-({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}1) \\\\  & =375-({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}375-({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}1) & =375-(10\\cdot 25) \\\\  & =375-250 \\\\  & =125.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{25}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}-1)=125.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149670" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "640efeb508dfb43c2554d4d361c3677898932e82d50175856399e8b5cf2882bb"} {"question" "q-149670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "120"] ["math" "125"] ["math" "130"] ["math" "135"] ["math" "145"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149670" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "125"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1+{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}=25,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij}=20.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1+{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}2{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+25+40 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+65 & =8\\cdot 10+65 \\\\  & =80+65 \\\\  & =145.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1+{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij})=145.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "640efeb508dfb43c2554d4d361c3677898932e82d50175856399e8b5cf2882bb"} {"question" "q-149675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "120"] ["math" "125"] ["math" "135"] ["math" "145"] ["math" "150"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "145"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}+1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}=20,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}=10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({a}_{i}+1)({b}_{j}+1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({b}_{j}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}({a}_{i}+1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}({b}_{j}+1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}{a}_{i}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1) \\\\  & =(20+15)\\cdot (10+10) \\\\  & =(35)\\cdot (20) \\\\  & =700.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149678" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "640efeb508dfb43c2554d4d361c3677898932e82d50175856399e8b5cf2882bb"} {"question" "q-149678" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149678" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "400"] ["math" "500"] ["math" "600"] ["math" "700"] ["math" "800"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14075200/state.json" "file_sha256" "de4fe60a3f20f24dabaa49ce29a086e80c662715c0811c9d88effb97d5128383"} {"question" "q-149678" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "700"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question